  "completed_behaviors": [
    "Unpaid offline orders omit the refund instructions. Paid unshipped offline orders can be cancelled, release stock, and record a pending refund exactly once.",
    "Supplier consent is bound to exact terms. Bank-transfer checkout freezes supplier terms; authorized suppliers read only shipping recipient data and supply costs, then record shipment or inability to ship.",
    "Supplier inability links to the original seller order for cancellation/refund. Cancellation closes the exception atomically; shipment versus cancellation has one winner and one inventory effect.",
    "The 180-day retention path removes recipient and tracking data from buyer, seller and supplier views while preserving shipment facts.",
    "Ordinary shipping quote shapes remain compatible. Drop-shipping uses strict UTC millisecond timestamps and the shared mixed-shipper reason vocabulary."
